<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oaxaca</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oaxaca is a state of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> on the Pacific coast, with its capital at Oaxaca de Juárez. Its mountains and valleys were home to the Zapotec and Mixtec civilisations, including the city of Monte Albán, and the region was conquered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztecs</a> in the 15th century and by the Spanish in the 1520s. It has one of the largest Indigenous populations in Mexico.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oaxaca.jpg" alt="Oaxaca" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Prsjl · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oaxaqa_(41).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
